    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0170" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5213</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Russia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-09T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1472. Your 1373, June 7, 8 p.m. President’s communication being given to press
                    for publication morning papers June 10 without alteration. The President desires
                    me to express to the Provisional <pb facs="0171" n="97" xml:id="pg97"/>
                    Government of Russia his gratification at the way it has received his
                    communication and is especially pleased that the Russian authorities appreciate
                    the spirit which inspired it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
